From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jon Pretty <jon.pretty@propensive.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:25:51 +0200
Subject: Make the synthetic jdk.internal.ValueBased annotation class permanent

Under -release (ct.sym), jdk.internal.ValueBased is absent and upstream
#27318 has Definitions.JdkInternalValueBasedAnnot synthesize a class symbol
for it, which the classfile parser then attaches to every @ValueBased JDK
class (Integer, Long, Optional, ...). Definitions is shared by every run of
a compiler instance, but the symbol was created with newCompleteClassSymbol
and never entered in its owner, so it is valid only in the run that made
it: in the next run, any look at those classes' annotations -- the
backend's isScalaStatic check when boxing, for one -- brings it forward,
stillValid fails, and compilation crashes with a StaleSymbolException. A
second run happens whenever a unit is suspended for a macro defined in the
same compilation, and in the REPL. Building scala3-repl itself crashed this
way in genBCode on Fansi.scala.

Mark the symbol Permanent, as every other synthetic class in Definitions
is (newPermanentClassSymbol, enterCompleteClassSymbol), so stillValid
accepts it in every run. Upstream candidate.

Developed with LLM assistance (Claude).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Proscala-Patch: valuebased
---
 compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/core/Definitions.scala | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/core/Definitions.scala b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/core/Definitions.scala
index 2bac0cdea94b64f8009b7c0b58de3e6504f53148..c44e67dea154eab98a3c4371050b3769e6c7d684 100644
--- a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/core/Definitions.scala
+++ b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/core/Definitions.scala
@@ -1225,7 +1225,9 @@ class Definitions {
   @tu lazy val JdkInternalValueBasedAnnot: Symbol = getClassIfDefined("jdk.internal.ValueBased").orElse {
     val pkg = getPackageClassIfDefined("jdk.internal")
     if pkg.exists then
-      val flags = JavaDefined | JavaAnnotation | PureInterfaceCreationFlags | Abstract
+      // Permanent: `Definitions` outlives a run, and a symbol created here but entered
+      // nowhere is otherwise stale in the next run (compilation-suspension restarts, REPL).
+      val flags = JavaDefined | JavaAnnotation | PureInterfaceCreationFlags | Abstract | Permanent
       completeClass(newCompleteClassSymbol(pkg, "ValueBased".toTypeName, flags, List(ObjectType, JavaAnnotationClass.typeRef), newScope))
     else NoSymbol
   }
